From 06847ca896625a3a690d8d40dcf94924b3bd9836 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:00:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-94: Blend's sizing and zoom shortcuts (0.94.0)

Blend (Keyboard shortcuts): "Make the selected objects the same width /
height / size: Ctrl+Shift+1 / 2 / 9", "Zoom in / out: Ctrl+= / Ctrl+-", "Fit
the selection to the screen size: Ctrl+0 (Ctrl+9)", "View the artboard at
actual size: Ctrl+1". These were only on the right-click menu and the
artboard toolbar. Now the 8 keys run align.width / height / size, the new
zoomIn / zoomOut (a zoomStep = the toolbar's + / -), zoomSelection and
resetZoom -- only while the design surface itself has the focus and F2's
text box is not open (elsewhere they stay VS Code's: Ctrl+= zooms the window).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 159, smoke 184, panels, real VS Code 157):
smoke (the 8 keys, their commands and when; zoomIn / zoomOut send one step
each); probe (zoomStep 1 -> 1.1 -> 1). The real VS Code layer failed once on
"rename (real) ... selected" (the form got selected after an extra redraw,
32 renders instead of 31) and passed on the rerun (157/0); this change does
not touch renaming.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
